{"tool_name":"bcforms","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"bcforms","home":"https://www.bcforms.org","license":"MIT","summary":"BcForms is a toolkit for concretely describing the molecular structure (atoms and bonds) of macromolecular complexes, including non-canonical monomeric forms, circular topologies, and crosslinks.\n\nBcForms includes a grammar for describing forms of macromolecular complexes composed of DNA, RNA, protein, and small molecular subunits and crosslinks between the subunits. The DNA, RNA, and protein subunits can be described using BpForms and the small molecule subunits can be described using SMILES. BcForms also includes four software tools for verifying descriptions of complexes and calculating physical properties of complexes such as their molecular structure, formula, molecular weight, and charge: a web application, a JSON REST API, a command line interface, and a Python API.","addition_date":"2020-05-22T17:01:47Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:35:21.390013Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library","Web API","Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:bcforms","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"karr@mssm.edu","name":"Jonathan Karr","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2605-5080","typeEntity":"Person","url":"https://www.karrlab.org"}],"documentation":[{"type":["API documentation"],"url":"https://docs.karrlab.org/bcforms"},{"type":["API documentation"],"url":"https://www.bcforms.org/api"},{"type":["Training material"],"url":"https://sandbox.karrlab.org/tree/bcforms"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://www.bcforms.org"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Protein structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1460"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Protein comparison","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2997"},{"term":"Protein property calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0250"},{"term":"Sequence conversion","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0233"},{"term":"Sequence visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0564"},{"term":"Validation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2428"}]}],"maturity":"Emerging","name":"BcForms","owner":"jonrkarr","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-020-02025-z","metadata":{"abstract":"Non-canonical residues, caps, crosslinks, and nicks are important to many functions of DNAs, RNAs, proteins, and complexes. However, we do not fully understand how networks of such non-canonical macromolecules generate behavior. One barrier is our limited formats for describing macromolecules. To overcome this barrier, we develop BpForms and BcForms, a toolkit for representing the primary structure of macromolecules as combinations of residues, caps, crosslinks, and nicks. The toolkit can help omics researchers perform quality control and exchange information about macromolecules, help systems biologists assemble global models of cells that encompass processes such as post-translational modification, and help bioengineers design cells.","authors":[{"name":"Chebaro Y."},{"name":"Karr J.R."},{"name":"Lang P.F."},{"name":"Natale D.A."},{"name":"P. Sekar J.A."},{"name":"Shaikh B."},{"name":"Zheng X."}],"citationCount":7,"date":"2020-05-18T00:00:00Z","journal":"Genome Biology","title":"BpForms and BcForms: A toolkit for concretely describing non-canonical polymers and complexes to facilitate global biochemical networks"},"pmcid":"PMC7236495","pmid":"32423472","type":["Method"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Biochemistry","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3292"},{"term":"Biochemistry","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3292"},{"term":"Chemical biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3369"},{"term":"Epigenomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3173"},{"term":"Genetics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3053"},{"term":"Nucleic acids","uri":"htt